@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-task-ids-are-sequential-per-list-and-win-over-titles
+type: decision-log
+title: "Task ids are sequential per list, and win over titles"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks need a reference that survives a rename. The domain may not read the clock or make random values
+(r3), so ids cannot be timestamps or random.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Ids are `task-<n>`, from a counter kept by each list. The counter never goes back, so an id is not
+  reused after a removal.
+- Where a key could be an id or a title, the id is tried first, then the title.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Ids are deterministic but unique only within a list.
+- A task whose title equals another task's id (e.g. "task-1") can only be reached by its title when no
+  task has that id.
